strings |id, value|

bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    web_gpu_layout_grid_px_tracks_never_admitted_2026-11-27, 0, "_web_layout_append_tracks (gpu_web/layout/adapter.spl:111) reads each stored track token with token.to_i64(); on seed fb80903917d6d5f5 '40px'.to_i64() and '1fr'.to_i64() are 0, so every px/fr template returns supported:false, and an empty template has count 0. Either way the grid gets LAYOUT_GPU_ADMISSION_UNSUPPORTED_TRACK, so no grid is ever GPU-admitted."
    web_gpu_layout_grid_px_tracks_never_admitted_2026-11-27, 1, "Measured through web_layout_adapt_cpu_oracle on base 3543da84e51 and head: rows/cols ''/'40px 40px', '20px'/'40px 40px', ''/'40px 1fr', ''/'1fr 1fr', '20px 20px'/'40px 1fr' all give flags & UNSUPPORTED_TRACK = 256. '40'.to_i64() = 40. test/01_unit/browser_engine/grid_auto_rows_gpu_admission_spec.spl (grid lane) pins parity, not admission, for this reason."
    web_gpu_layout_grid_px_tracks_never_admitted_2026-11-27, 2, "Repro: simple_web_layout_render_html_draw_ir_result('<div style='display:grid;grid-template-columns:40px 40px'><div>a</div><div>b</div></div>', 320, 240) -> web_layout_adapt_cpu_oracle(browser, 1, layout_execution_profile('serial_cpu', 50, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0), 4); the grid node's semantics.gpu_admission_flags & LAYOUT_GPU_ADMISSION_UNSUPPORTED_TRACK is 256."

